	// rather than as an `importCall(slot IatSlot, …)` in the `call` band. Two independent reasons,
	// and both are load-bearing:
	//
	// 1. **TIERING.** `IatSlot` is a WINDOWS PE concept (`Targets/Windows/PeWriter.maxon`), and it
	//    is referenced nowhere outside `Targets/`. Naming it here would put a PE import-table index
	//    in the target-NEUTRAL mid-level tier — the tier ARCHITECTURE says the wasm backend will
	//    consume directly. `osAllocPages` says WHAT is wanted (pages) and lets each backend say HOW
	//    (x64-windows: `VirtualAlloc` through the IAT; Linux: `mmap`; wasm: `memory.grow`). BOTH
	//    reference compilers independently refuse the leak: v1 has `std osAllocPages <size>`, and
	//    the bootstrap has `IEmitterBackend.OsAllocPages` with `VirtualAlloc` appearing in zero
